[list]
[*]Moving a stand keeps its owner. Reinstalling one anywhere else used to clear the owner without saying so, leaving what looked like an owned stand open to the whole colony. Its work types, its change-the-whole-outfit setting and the Allow removing items lock all come through the move as well.
[*]Moving a stand while somebody has its uniform out no longer strands their clothes. Their own clothes travel inside the crate with the stand, and when you set it back down they can change back exactly as before. Previously the stand came out of the crate treating those clothes as part of its own outfit, so the colonist stayed in the uniform for good and their own clothes became stand stock.
[*]A colonist is never locked into a uniform by a stand that does not come back. While a stand is packed up, the uniform stops counting as forced, so the usual clothing rules can replace it if the crate is sold, burnt or simply left in storage. Setting the stand back down restores the shift as it stood.
[/list]
